---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { pathTo } from '../lib/paths';
const questions = [
  ['Is it really free?', 'The initial assessment is free. Most other services are free or low cost. Custom software is a paid engagement, and website hosting and infrastructure costs are paid by the client. We agree on scope and any cost before work begins.'],
  ['Who does the work?', 'Marist students, organized by specialty, with faculty support. We are a student-led program, not an ongoing managed IT service.'],
  ['Will you need my passwords or client data?', 'No. We never ask for passwords or client records. Assessments are scoped and approved in writing first, and we’re glad to sign an NDA. Please don’t send sensitive information through our forms.'],
  ['We already have an IT company. Can you still help?', 'Yes. We give an independent second look and can share results with your existing IT company. We can discuss how to coordinate during the initial call.'],
  ['How long does an assessment take?', 'It depends on the size of your organization and the agreed scope. We begin with a 20-minute conversation, then confirm a realistic schedule with you before work starts.'],
  ['What happens after the assessment?', 'You receive a checklist and a plain-English summary report with quick wins and bigger risks. Then you decide whether you want help with anything else. There is no commitment to a follow-on project.'],
  ['Do you offer emergency support?', 'No. We do not offer 24/7 emergency support or ongoing managed IT contracts. For urgent or ongoing needs, we’ll refer you to a local provider.'],
];
---
<Layout title="Frequently asked questions" description="Answers about Marist Tech Clinic assessment costs, student teams, privacy, timelines, existing IT providers and the limits of our support." page="/faq/">
  <div class="container"><header class="page-intro"><p class="page-kicker">Frequently asked questions</p><h1>Let’s clear a few things up.</h1><p class="lead">What to expect before, during, and after working with the clinic.</p></header><div class="faq-layout"><aside class="faq-aside"><h2>Another question?</h2><p>Tell us what you’re wondering about. We’re happy to talk it through.</p><a class="text-link" href={pathTo('/contact/')}>Send us a message</a></aside><div class="faq-list">{questions.map(([question, answer]) => <details><summary>{question}</summary><p>{answer}</p></details>)}</div></div></div>
</Layout>
